{"id": "EUVD-2026-103859", "enisaUuid": "bc23c30e-c1ce-33f9-9246-f6c592d53017", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrust_binder: cancel deferred work items in thread exit\n\nIf there are deferred work items on the thread todo list, then they are\nnot cleaned up in the Thread::release() method. Thus, update the code to\nclean up the work items even if they are deferred.\n\nThis can happen if the thread dies while it has an active outgoing\ntransaction.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:25:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d54df2de22f9ac5b660d0ec898986f805e97c096", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98dc9fababd1b7fb1a88b8362183baa5779c2394", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62479b6e5df82cbdf3c4145130928f233fae78fb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98774", "GHSA-3hmp-3v2x-8x2w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2fc0b602-a27a-381c-aa90-0417b19d5da9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "425c9b58-c189-3170-b535-0c23a8db428d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eafedbc7c050c44744fbdf80bdf3315e860b7513 <d54df2de22f9ac5b660d0ec898986f805e97c096"}, {"id": "b58f150d-fb16-34ec-8726-195d427f0fb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eafedbc7c050c44744fbdf80bdf3315e860b7513 <62479b6e5df82cbdf3c4145130928f233fae78fb"}, {"id": "c86028e8-8eb0-31c6-9728-b8a4872dc39a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "cc1fec11-ebc2-323c-9f86-b3283a80c4ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "faf9570c-02a8-366a-b3af-a2516b2d8426", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "fe3f64a4-57e1-3c31-91df-75fbe5fefcb5", "produc